 "text": "You can now edit videos by just talking to Claude Code.\n\nSave this before you pay another editor for a simple cut.\n\nThe team behind Browser Use just open-sourced a skill called video-use.\n\nYou drop your footage in a folder and describe the edit in plain English.\n\nIt transcribes every word with timestamps, finds the silences, and cuts on word boundaries, so nothing gets chopped mid-sentence.\n\nRetakes, filler words, dead air: gone. Then it grades the color, burns in captions, and drops in B-roll where it makes sense.\n\nI ran my own ad footage through it. It found the clean take, removed the stutters, and rendered the finished cut in seconds.\n\nAnd it remembers every decision in a project file, so the next edit starts where the last one ended.\n\nFree. Open source. Runs on your own Mac.\n\nFollow for more free AI tools I actually use.",
